<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-peru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Peru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Peru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Juan Velasco Alvarado seizes power and begins radical reforms</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-panama"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Panama.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Panama</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The National Guard overthrows Arnulfo Arias, beginning military rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Warsaw Pact armies invade to end the Prague Spring</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ebla"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ebla.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ebla</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A statue of King Ibbit-Lim identifies Tell Mardikh as Ebla</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Arab%20Emirates.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Arab Emirates</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zayed and Rashid agree to form a union after Britain announces its withdrawal from the Gulf</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swazi%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swazi Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Swaziland becomes independent under Sobhuza II</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/civil-rights-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Civil%20rights%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Civil rights movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Martin Luther King Jr. is assassinated in Memphis, and Congress passes the Fair Housing Act</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/clovis-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Clovis%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Clovis culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Anzick-1 burial is found near Wilsall, Montana</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/malay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Malay becomes the sole official language of Peninsular Malaysia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The People's Army of Vietnam and the Việt Cộng launch the Tet Offensive, which fails militarily but marks a turning point in US support</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/hue"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hu%E1%BA%BF.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Huế</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">North Vietnamese and Việt Cộng forces occupy most of Huế in the Tết Offensive; the city is retaken after a month of fighting</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/abu-simbel"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Abu%20Simbel.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Abu Simbel</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The relocated complex was finished and formally inaugurated on 22 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/tomb-of-tutankhamun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tomb%20of%20Tutankhamun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tomb of Tutankhamun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A theft from the sarcophagus after 1926 came to light when the anatomist Ronald Harrison re-examined the remains</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Shot at the Lorraine Motel in Memphis on 4 April and dies the same evening</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alexander Dubček replaces Antonín Novotný as First Secretary of the Communist Party on 5 January</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dubček launches the Action Programme of liberalisations in April, under the slogan of &quot;socialism with a human face&quot;</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The talks at Čierna nad Tisou and the Bratislava Declaration end with a compromise that the Soviet leadership soon abandons</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Warsaw Pact troops invade on the night of 20–21 August, and Dubček is arrested and taken to Moscow</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/american-indian-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/American%20Indian%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>American Indian Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">AIM is founded in Minneapolis, and the Minneapolis AIM Patrol is created to monitor police treatment of urban American Indians</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Iraqi Ba'ath seizes power in a coup and later gives asylum to Aflaq</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzania begins consolidating its rural population into village communities, a programme that runs to 1975</span></li></ul></section>
